cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "FCDI-BES life-cycle and techno-economic assessment: input data and calculation code"
abstract: "Input data (versioned CSV tables with a provenance record for every row) and the Python package that
  performs every calculation of a cradle-to-gate life cycle assessment and techno-economic assessment of selenium
  treatment by flow-electrode capacitive deionization coupled to bio-electrochemical systems (FCDI-BES), with the
  runner that validates the inputs and reproduces every result table. The licensed ecoinvent 3.7 factors are not
  included: a factor template, a dummy factor table and a flow dictionary are provided, and all techno-economic
  results are reproduced without a license. Code: MIT License; data: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA)."
type: software
